        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: drain inbound debounce buffer and followup queues before SIGUSR1 reload",
        "body": "Related: #51620\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users whose inbound message was accepted shortly before a SIGUSR1 or config reload could have buffered message content silently dropped before it reached the reply pipeline.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe gateway now closes ordinary work admission synchronously, flushes accepted inbound debounce work inside one core-private restart continuation, drains channel, active-turn, and followup work in order, then rechecks work created by followup delivery. Pre-created debounce callbacks are explicitly rebound to the private restart admission context, while the global sweep is bounded by both the remaining restart deadline and a 100-pass/30-second ceiling so continued ingress cannot stall reload indefinitely.\n\nForced restarts retain the existing skip-drain behavior. This does not persist messages sent while the gateway is offline.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMessages accepted immediately before an in-process reload can complete through the normal command/reply path instead of being rejected by the restart fence or disappearing from in-memory buffers. A sustained stream of new transport events also cannot hold the gateway forever in the debounce-flush phase.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact-head validation for `c9067e7397281341627e8fdef266b7b865ff6101`:\n\n- **Focused behavior tests:** 3 files, 148 tests passed.\n  - `src/auto-reply/inbound.test.ts`: 65 passed.\n  - `src/process/command-queue.test.ts`: 40 passed.\n  - `src/cli/gateway-cli/run-loop.test.ts`: 43 passed.\n- **New P1 regressions:** a buffer task created before restart successfully enqueues real command work only after being flushed from the private restart continuation; continuous ingress stops at the pass cap; the exact final-pass boundary reports drained correctly; a slow callback returns at the supplied deadline.\n- **Formatting/lint:** `oxfmt --check` and type-aware `oxlint --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.core.json` passed on all touched files.\n- **Type safety:** core production, core test, and plugin SDK declaration `tsgo` checks passed.\n- **Tree identity:** GitHub tree `05b44e3f161d904f3816bc5351ae6d9d5e384443` is the exact locally tested tree; all five uploaded blob SHAs matched the local Git objects.\n- **CI:** GitHub Actions is running on the exact head above.\n\nA live Signal/Telegram account is not paired in this environment. I have requested the repository's Mantis Telegram proof flow below so maintainers can attach redacted channel-to-gateway reload evidence to this exact head.\n\n## Implementation and Safety Notes\n\n- `createInboundDebouncer()` retains its public `enqueue` / `flushKey` / `cancelKey` return shape.\n- `ChannelRunQueue` retains its public `enqueue` / `deactivate` shape.\n- No public `enqueueInternal`, `allowDuringGatewayDrain`, or command-queue admission bypass is exposed.\n- The debounce registry is weak, avoiding channel teardown requirements.\n- Overflow-summary backlog is included in followup pending counts.\n- The branch remains a focused 13-file change.\n\n## Synchronization\n\n- **PR head:** `c9067e7397281341627e8fdef266b7b865ff6101`\n- **Immediate parent:** `1952ec24195d85e8f6ea032fe76b44806d952f69`\n- **Synchronized main cutoff:** `262baedcf7fa3d66dc35cce7d0253e0a31f0cc0e`\n- **Cutoff merge topology:** synchronization commit `5ae09ec76ee9b851cb24b07acad291724c185868` has first parent `da4b1b9c15b6a7b965657fc753e0c25d8dd0e4fa` and second parent `262baedcf7fa3d66dc35cce7d0253e0a31f0cc0e`.\n- **Diff:** 13 files, +893/-130.\n",
        "branch": "fix/drain-queue-before-sigusr1",
